{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793383727,"nonce":"rUrZhrJ1And8hKmTzlclUZ8BulU=","message":"Rayzor side of display-mode completion landed in 42bb750a.\n- Compiler: Compiler.getDisplayPos, Context.containsDisplayPosition and getDisplayMode report a thread-local display cursor (macro_system/display.rs). EDisplay lowers to reserved `$display.\u003ckind\u003e` metadata; typing records the wrapped expression's type, or for DKStructure the expected type, e.g. from an enclosing ECheckType. In a display compile, build fields carry named-file positions so getPosInfos/containsDisplayPosition can place the cursor.\n- LSP: a completion request whose cursor is inside a markup token starts a display compile in a fresh unit on a separate task. Its last DKDot/DKStructure request is answered with the type's fields; with none, the ordinary path answers. `\u003c`, `/` and space are trigger characters, answered empty outside markup.\n- Tested by an LSP session fixture that mirrors Ashui's two shapes. Not yet run against real Ashui, which needs its sibling checkouts.\nRemaining:\n- tag completion while the tag is unterminated (the lexer rejects the file, so no markup token is found) needs the tolerant markup scanner;\n- Tw class completion from ashui.style.Tw.completions() is not consumed;\n- quoted attribute values are not completed.","files":null}]}